hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19168","Qutayba narrated to us: Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Nafi ibn Kaysan, that his father informed him that he used to trade in wine in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and that he came from Sham with wine in wineskins seeking trade. So he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have brought you a good drink. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Kaysan, it has been forbidden after you. He said: Shall I sell it, O Messenger of Allah? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It has been forbidden and its price has been forbidden. So Kaysan went to the wineskins, seized their legs, then poured it out."
